; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Four-Sided Shapes
; CATEGORY: Shapes & Polygons
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     quadrilateral, angles, rhombus, kite, trapezoid
; SUMMARY:  Draws the six famous quadrilaterals side by side and labels each one.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Square, rectangle, rhombus, parallelogram, trapezoid and kite,
;   each in its own color with its name below. Every one of them
;   has four sides, and in every one the turns add up to 360.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Each shape is its own procedure, so you can type
;   rhombus 100 45  or  kite 60 120  in the command center.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * different four-sided shapes come from different angles and lengths
;   * opposite turns that add to 180 give parallel sides
;   * procedures with more than one input
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make a rhombus with a 90 degree angle. Which shape is it now?
;   * Draw a parallelogram with angle 90. What do you get?
;   * Add up the four turns in KITE. Do they make 360?
; ============================================================

to square :side
  repeat 4 [forward :side right 90]
end

to rectangle :width :height
  repeat 2 [forward :height right 90 forward :width right 90]
end

; A rhombus is a squashed square: all four sides are equal,
; but the corners are not right angles. The two turns, :angle and
; 180 - :angle, add up to 180, which keeps opposite sides parallel.
; We walk along the bottom first and turn LEFT so the shape grows upward.
to rhombus :side :angle
  right 90
  repeat 2 [forward :side left :angle forward :side left 180 - :angle]
  left 90
end

; A parallelogram is a squashed rectangle.
to parallelogram :width :height :angle
  right 90
  repeat 2 [forward :width left :angle forward :height left 180 - :angle]
  left 90
end

; A trapezoid has one pair of parallel sides, the top and bottom.
; We walk the long bottom, go up a slanted side, along the short top,
; then use SETXY to come back down to where we started.
to trapezoid :bottom :top :height
  localmake "x xcor localmake "y ycor
  setheading 90
  forward :bottom
  setxy :x + (:bottom + :top) / 2 :y + :height
  setxy :x + (:bottom - :top) / 2 :y + :height
  setxy :x :y
  setheading 0
end

; A kite: two short sides on top, two long sides below.
; We find the four corners from the middle line of the kite.
to kite :short :long
  localmake "x xcor localmake "y ycor
  setxy :x - :short * 0.7 :y + :long * 0.7
  setxy :x :y + :long * 0.7 + :short * 0.7
  setxy :x + :short * 0.7 :y + :long * 0.7
  setxy :x :y
end

to place :x :y :color :name
  penup setxy :x - 30 :y - 30 setheading 0
  setpencolor 0 label :name
  setxy :x :y pendown
  setpencolor :color
end

clearscreen
setpensize 3
setlabelheight 16

place -320 80 1 "square
square 100
place -80 80 4 "rectangle
rectangle 150 90
place 170 80 2 "rhombus
rhombus 100 60

place -330 -200 13 "parallelogram
parallelogram 150 90 60
place -50 -200 14 "trapezoid
trapezoid 160 80 100
place 250 -200 5 "kite
kite 70 140
hideturtle
